BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Strahl Lake Hike\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260905T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260905T094500
UID:14774efa29c7cddcafadbd7871fdf297@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist for a guided hike of Trail 6 around Lak
 e Strahl! Hear about the history of the lake\, the surrounding Strahl Vall
 ey\, and learn about the animals that make it their home. The section of T
 rail 6 around Lake Strahl is considered easy to moderate. It has some shor
 t staircases\, uneven surfaces\, and wet spots. The trail is less than a m
 ile and will take about 45 minutes to complete.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Lake Strahl parking lot\, 1405 S.R. 46 
 W\, Nashville\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Woodpeckers of Indiana\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260905T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260905T114500
UID:f0e8d64c7ae50b5ba86eaf424a85b52c@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join park expert\, bird enthusiast\, and NPR&#39\;s &quot\;Mom
 ent of Science&quot\; radio personality Don Glass in a presentation and di
 scussion about Indiana&#39\;s seven species of native woodpeckers! Learn w
 hat they look like\, their behaviors\, and some of the issues they face to
 day.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
