 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Timber! Understanding the Timber Rattlesnake\, Brown County State 
 Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260912T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260912T133000
UID:8145f5e36d725d7b8b7a97940c753a4d@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Come to the Nature Center for an up close and personal look In
 diana&#39\;s most venomous and most misunderstood snake! Learn about the h
 istory of timber rattlesnakes\, including how this animal became an Americ
 an symbol in the late 1700s. Learn how over a million visitors a year safe
 ly share the state park with these animals. We&#39\;ll also discuss venom\
 , how it works and is delievered\, and how Indiana&#39\;s venomous snakes 
 compare to the rest of the world! At the end\, we will feed the timber rat
 tlesnake a live mouse. Please be aware this program involves live animals.
  A live snake feeding may not be suitable for all guests\, particuarly chi
 ldren. Guests will have an opportunity to leave the program before the fee
 ding\, if they choose to do so. The program room has seating for about 45 
 people maximum. On busy days\, it is wise to arrive early!
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Trees From Seed\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260912T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260912T160000
UID:833e27df94be5bbe3c5b89529d8832e4@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join the park naturalist for a presentation created with the a
 ssistance of Ray Major. Ray is the man behind the &quot\;Trees From Seed&q
 uot\; social media movement\; this is an informative session on growing tr
 ees\, followed by a hike! Ray Major of Trees From Seed has a forestry degr
 ee from Purdue University and years of experience in forest management in 
 Indiana. Learn how to empower yourself to grow trees on your own\, hear ho
 w to protect young trees\, and get advice on which species of trees are co
 rrect for your property. Program is at Ogle Lake\, followed by an optional
  hike. For more information on growing trees\, visit https://www.facebook.
 com/Treesfromseed
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
