BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Autumn Leaves Revisited\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260925T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260925T154500
UID:ed905fc0b14a4d838ea37efda084d727@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered how and why our forests change into the
 ir beautiful fall colors? This program explains just that! Join a naturali
 st as we walk through how leaves transform through the seasons and why the
 y turn into the colors we see in the fall on the microscopic level! Stick 
 around after the program for a fun coloring activity to help you recognize
  and remember what changes our green leaves into yellows\, oranges\, reds\
 , and browns.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center program room\, 1405 S.R. 
 46 W\, Nashville\, IN 
URL:on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Backyard Birdfeeding\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260926T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260926T113000
UID:8e4ed06d45881d8fe6d9baeb14942e2c@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist for a presentation and discussion of ba
 ckyard bird feeding.&nbsp\; When should you feed and what should you feed 
 them? What type of feeders are best and where should you place them? Why d
 o we feed them\, and do we &quot\;need&quot\; to? Find out answers to thes
 e questions and more\, then view birds for yourself out the Wildlife Windo
 w at the Nature Center!
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/BrownCountySP
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Timber! Understanding the Timber Rattlesnake\, Brown County State 
 Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260926T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260926T163000
UID:13ad0f3ae0e6943490befc0762940148@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Come to the Nature Center for an up close and personal look In
 diana&#39\;s most venomous and most misunderstood snake! Learn about the h
 istory of timber rattlesnakes\, including how this animal became an Americ
 an symbol in the late 1700s. Learn how over a million visitors a year safe
 ly share the state park with these animals. We&#39\;ll also discuss venom\
 , how it works and is delievered\, and how Indiana&#39\;s venomous snakes 
 compare to the rest of the world! At the end\, we will feed the timber rat
 tlesnake a live mouse. Please be aware this program involves live animals.
  A live snake feeding may not be suitable for all guests\, particuarly chi
 ldren. Guests will have an opportunity to leave the program before the fee
 ding\, if they choose to do so. The program room has seating for about 45 
 people maximum. On busy days\, it is wise to arrive early!
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Campfire Storytime\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260926T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260926T184500
UID:aef7b4c60a8fcf131a4ac8e5d0f8c5e7@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join the nature center mascots\, Olive the Owl and Doug the De
 er\, and a park naturalist for a story reading. We will read Mossy &nbsp\;
 by Jan Brett or another title and enjoy a small campfire at the edge of th
 e woods. Meet at the fire ring behind the Friends&#39\; Shelterhouse near 
 the Nature Center. Come early to enjoy the fire if you like! We will take 
 suggestions on kid friendly books about nature! Feel free to suggest a fav
 orite of yours to the naturalist! Owl Moon \, The Lorax \, Mossy \, and Ze
 e Grows A Tree are popular titles\, but we&#39\;d love to add more variety
 !
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center (Friends' Circle)\, 1405 
 S.R. 46 W\, Nashville\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260926T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260926T203000
UID:d0b38f4b6d080ff34d5cdb28a2920016@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist for a guided night hike on the Salt Cre
 ek Trail! The Full Moon is the brightest night of the month\, leading to i
 nteresting views along the creek. Learn about September&#39\;s full moon t
 his year\, the Harvest Moon. The Salt Creek Trail is rated very easy\, but
  should be considered moderate in the dark. The trail has some minor slope
 s\, a short stretch of lawn\, and possible wet or icy spots depending on w
 eather. Our route is&nbsp\; about 2 miles total and will take about an hou
 r to complete. Please do not bring pets on night hikes. Red flashlights ar
 e preferred for night vision and can be loaned to hikers on request. Hike 
 cancellation policy : Hikes will be cancelled if there is lightning\, temp
 eratures below 0 degrees Farenheit\, temperature indexes above 105 degrees
  Farenheit\, or a wind advisory. If a hike is cancelled\, gatehouses will 
 be informed. The phone number for the North Gatehouse is 812-988-5230.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Olympic Pool parking lot\, 1405 S.R. 46
  W\, Nashville\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/BrownCountySP
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
